{"ts": "2026-11-03T09:01:21.043560Z", "run_id": "r-20261103T0849Z-634b", "unit": "openspec:add-dbos-runtime", "seq": 34, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "Read the test: the query is at line 392 (within three lines of the cited 395) and asserts count 0 of stack.ready rows, matching the spec scenario \"ursitoare_e2e holds no stack.ready row\". No other repository query names a workflow_name column; the other suites filter workflow_status by workflow_uuid, application_version and queue_name, and the runtime maps the SDK's workflowName field, not a column. The SDK is not vendored in this checkout (node_modules absent, no junit report), so the column name rests on the DBOS system schema, where workflow_status has carried the workflow name in the `name` column in every release, and the lockfile pins 5.3.0. A wrong column would keep the test red with 42703 rather than let it pass falsely, so the downside of the edit is bounded. The clarifier suggestion changes only the column name in the frozen test, so accept.", "called": true, "tasks": ["5.2"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.4020259999999998, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "ef970fcc7163590ce4945543f11b13db9ddaaca547d79f6beb3871ab142aa709", "checked": [{"ref": "test/support/e2e-stack/durable-part.test.ts:392", "quote": "FROM dbos.workflow_status WHERE workflow_name = 'stack.ready'", "claim": "The frozen test filters the DBOS system table on a workflow_name column."}, {"ref": "test/support/e2e-stack/durable-part.test.ts:394", "quote": "the e2e database holds no stack.ready row", "claim": "The assertion's only intent is that no stack.ready row exists, so renaming the column keeps its meaning."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/durable-runtime/spec.md#scenario-ready-late-failed", "quote": "`ursitoare_e2e` holds no `stack.ready` row", "claim": "The specification requires only the absence of a stack.ready row, not a particular column name."}, {"ref": "src/durable/workflows.test.ts:210", "quote": "SELECT application_version, queue_name FROM dbos.workflow_status WHERE workflow_uuid = 'w-2'", "claim": "The other suites filter workflow_status by its real columns and none uses workflow_name."}, {"ref": "src/durable/launch.ts:318", "quote": "workflow: found.workflowName", "claim": "The runtime reads the SDK status object's workflowName field; no repository code relies on a workflow_name column."}, {"ref": "pnpm-lock.yaml:142", "quote": "'@dbos-inc/dbos-sdk@5.3.0':", "claim": "The project pins DBOS 5.3.0, whose workflow_status table stores the workflow name in the name column."}]}
